# ============================================================================
# P03 - SCHEDULER: drop SCHED_AUTOGROUP      [EXPERIMENTAL / UNVERIFIED]
# ============================================================================
# WHAT IT CHANGES
#   CONFIG_SCHED_AUTOGROUP=y  ->  # CONFIG_SCHED_AUTOGROUP is not set
#
#   baseline evidence (kernel source, commit 9b1c9a53):
#     arch/arm64/configs/k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig:14   CONFIG_SCHED_AUTOGROUP=y
#     arch/arm64/configs/oppo6765_defconfig:9        CONFIG_SCHED_AUTOGROUP=y
#     (two independent MT6765 MTK/OPPO defconfigs agree - see cross-check)
#     Neighbouring Android-relevant group options are all present and stay:
#       CONFIG_UCLAMP_TASK=y, CONFIG_UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP=y, CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE=y
#       CONFIG_CPUSETS=y, CONFIG_BLK_CGROUP=y, CONFIG_MTK_SCHED_EXTENSION=y
#
# WHY IT SHOULD HELP ON A 4 GB MT6765V
#   SCHED_AUTOGROUP is the desktop session-isolation layer: on task creation
#   and group moves it allocates and links an autogroup per (task, session),
#   keeps a global autogroup list, and on every scheduling decision in
#   kernel/sched/fair.c the entity carries an extra autogroup pointer through
#   enqueue/dequeue/pick-next. Its Kconfig help describes it in terms of
#   "task group" isolation between login sessions - a TTY/desktop concept.
#   Android has no login sessions. Its grouping needs are already met by the
#   options listed above (cgroups+cpusets for affinity, SCHED_TUNE and
#   CONFIG_UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP for priority, MTK_SCHED_EXTENSION for the vendor
#   big-task placement logic). So autogroup here buys no policy that is used,
#   while its bookkeeping sits on the scheduling hot path and its per-task
#   objects are extra kernel memory on a 4 GB device.
#
#   NOTE ON HONESTY: the per-decision cost is a pointer dereference and a
#   conditional, not a large one. This patch is expected to be SMALL. It is
#   included because it is unambiguously dead weight for the platform, not
#   because a benchmark is expected to show anything dramatic. Do not expect
#   a measurable frame-time change.
#
# WHAT WOULD VERIFY OR REFUTE IT
#   Baseline vs patched, under a fixed repeatable interaction script:
#     dumpsys gfxinfo <pkg> framestats   (p50/p95 frame times, jank counts)
#     cat /proc/pressure/cpu
#     grep -E 'ctxt|processes' /proc/stat  (after the same fixed workload)
#   Refutation criterion: if p95 frame time and total context-switch count
#   are indistinguishable run-to-run, the patch is doing nothing observable
#   and should be dropped for simplicity rather than kept on faith.
#
# RISK
#   Only real risk is a vendor/userspace component that reads autogroup state.
#   Confirm nothing in the target ROM writes to or reads
#   /sys/kernel/debug/sched/... autogroup entries, or relies on
#   CONFIG_SCHED_AUTOGROUP. MTK's sched extensions do not use it.
# ============================================================================

# CONFIG_SCHED_AUTOGROUP is not set
